course: dictionary
lesson: 12776
title: Words for people who teach
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An educator is a person whose job is to teach or help people learn. You can find the clues in the words around it. «The museum educator showed us how clay pots were made.» A museum is a place to look at old things, and someone who shows you how things were made is helping you learn. So an educator is someone who teaches.
explain: Educate is the verb, meaning to teach. Add -or to show a person who does the job, so an educator educates. Other words with -or work the same way, like visitor, a person who visits.
explain: Educators can work in many places. «Parents and educators met to talk about reading at home.» Here, educators are people who work with children, such as teachers. A formal word like educators often shows up in news and serious writing, so it helps to know what it means.
fact: An educator is a person whose job is to teach or educate people.
fact: Teachers, tutors and lecturers are all kinds of educators.
fact: «Educators» means teachers and others who work in schools, in news and formal writing.
fact: A museum educator or zoo educator runs learning sessions for visitors.
fact: The word comes from the verb «educate», which means to teach, plus -or, which means a person who does the job.
exercise: «The museum educator showed us how clay pots were made.» What is a museum educator? | A cleaner who dusts the displays | *Someone who runs learning sessions for visitors | A guard who looks after the paintings | A person who sells tickets at the door
exercise: Find and copy the word that means people who teach or help children learn. «Parents and educators met to talk about reading at home.» | talk | parents | *educators | reading
exercise: Which of these is an educator? | A farmer who grows wheat | A bus driver who takes children to school | *A lecturer who teaches students at a university | A nurse who looks after patients
test: «In the news, educators asked for smaller classes.» Who are the educators in this sentence? | Bus drivers who take children home | A newsreader on television | *Teachers and others who work in schools | Children who go to school
test: What does educator mean? | A person who collects old books | A person whose job is to teach or help people learn | A person who sells food | *A person who builds houses
exam: «A zoo educator ran a session about owls, and the children took notes.» What is the zoo educator's job? | *To run learning sessions for visitors | To sell tickets at the gate | To clean the cages | To feed the animals at night
